                                                "sense_id": "d2495e22-881b-3770-bcb2-5b0463c23f91",
                                                "text": "In most American whalemen the mast-heads are manned almost simultaneously with the vessel’s leaving her port; even though she may have fifteen thousand miles, and more, to sail ere reaching her proper cruising ground."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
